Decoupled x and y:

Before, we already determined that
x(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l + theta_r)
y(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l - theta_r)
x'(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l' + theta_r') 
y'(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l' - theta_r')

Expanding this:
x''(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l'' + theta_r'') 
y''(theta_l,theta_r) = 0.5r_m(theta_l'' - theta_r'')

x'' = 0.5r_m(K_m i_ml / (J_m + 0.5m r_m^2) + K_m i_mr / (J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
= r_m K_m (i_ml + i_mr) / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
with (i_ml + i_mr)' = i_ml' + i_mr' = (u_ml+u_mr-R_m(i_ml+i_mr)) / L_m

Note that u_ml and u_mr are our inputs, and i_ml and i_mr are state variables.
Define a new input u_x = u_ml+u_mr and a new state variable i_x = i_ml+i_mr

The equations for x are simplified:
x'' = r_m K_m i_x / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
with i_x' = (u_x - R_m i_x) / L_m

Similarly for y:
y'' = 0.5r_m(K_m i_ml / (J_m + 0.5m r_m^2) - K_m i_mr / (J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
= r_m K_m (i_ml - i_mr) / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
with (i_ml - i_mr)' = i_ml' - i_mr' = (u_ml-u_mr-R_m(i_ml-i_mr)) / L_m

We can define u_y = u_ml-u_mr, i_y = i_ml - i_mr :
y'' = r_m K_m i_y / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
with i_y' = (u_y - R_m i_y) / L_m

We define state x_x = [x', x, i_x]^T, and x_y = [y', y, i_y]^T

x_x' = [x'', x', i_x']^T
with x'' = r_m K_m i_x / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
     x' = x'
     i_x' = (u_x - R_m i_x) / L_m

We arrive at a state-space description x_x' = f_x(x_x, u_x) = A_x x_x + B_x u_x
     
with A_x = [[0,             0, r_m K_m / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))],
            [1,             0,              0],
            [0,             0,         -R_m / L_m]]

     B_x = [0, 0, 1/L_m]^T

For x_y, similarly:
x_y' = [y'', y', i_y']^T
with y'' = r_m K_m i_y / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))
     y' = y'
     i_y' = (u_y - R_m i_y) / L_m

We arrive at a state-space description x_y' = f_y(x_y, u_y) = A_y x_y + B_y u_y

with A_y = A_x = [[0,             0, r_m K_m / (2(J_m + 0.5m r_m^2))],
                  [1,             0,              0],
                  [0,             0,         -R_m / L_m]]

     B_y = B_x = [0, 0, 1/L_m]^T












